# What the images' build context leaves out. Each Dockerfile copies only what it names (the server image: CMakeLists.txt,
# src/ and app/; the frontend image: src/oms-frontend/ and its nginx files), but the context is sent whole, so this
# keeps it small and keeps secrets out of it in case a Dockerfile ever copies more (#565). Patterns match from the root;
# **/ matches at any depth.
.git
src/oms-frontend/node_modules
src/oms-frontend/dist
src/oms-frontend/.vite
# Build trees at the root (build, build-asan, build-benchmark, ...), which run to gigabytes, and objects and archives
# anywhere
build*
**/*.o
**/*.a
# Runtime data, logs and benchmark baselines
data
**/exchange.log
benchmark_baseline*
# Secrets: the stack's environment (the WebSocket token, the Postgres password), its TLS key, and the identities: the
# WebSocket ones and the FIX counterparties'
docker/.env
docker/certs
docker/ws-credentials
docker/fix-credentials
docker/ws-identities
